---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { TEXT_COLORS } from "../../config/site";

// Add descriptors to the buttons
---

<Layout title="About | My Blog">
	<head>
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
		<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
		<link
			href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Merriweather:wght@300&display=swap"
			rel="stylesheet"
		/>
	</head>
	<!-- ugly styling unfortunately -->
	<article class="about-content" style={`--h2-color: ${TEXT_COLORS.Project};`}> 
		<header class="about-heading">
			<p class="title">About Me</p>
			<p class="subtitle">01/01/2026</p>
		</header>
		
		<section>
			<div class="about-hero">
				<div class="hero-left">
					<img
						src="/images/about/babel.jpg"
						alt="babel"
						class="hero-image"
					/>
				</div>

				<div class="hero-right">
					<h2>Who I Am</h2>
					<p>
						The author of this website is Andy Yao. I'm a software
						dev by trade, and studied at the University of Michigan.

						<br /><br />
						I tend to use the tower of Babel as a profile picture.
						<br />
						Credit goes to Pieter Bruegel the Elder, <a href="https://www.boijmans.nl/en/collection/in-depth/bruegel-s-tower-of-babel" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">c. 1563</a>
					</p>
				
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Get In Touch</h2>
			<p>
				The best way to reach me is via email: andyyao15 [at] gmail [dot] com
				<br>
				You can also find my resume, LinkedIn, and GitHub in the header above.
			</p>
			
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>What I Do</h2>
			<p>
				I'm currently a software developer at Palantir, working on the Mixed Reality team.
				<br />
				My interests include extended reality, sociology, and
				history.
				<br />
				In my free time, I tinker with various personal projects, read history/fantasy/sci-fi,
				and run.
				<br />
				<br />
				Also, did you know I happen to have a blog? :)
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Why This Blog?</h2>
			<p>
				This website serves as a portfolio of my work and a way to document
				my journey in life. I hope to share my experiences in such a way
				that others can learn from them.
				<br /><br />
					For more detail, check out this website's very own <a
						class="special-link"
						style={`--special-link-color: ${TEXT_COLORS.Thought};`}
						href="/post/about-this-website">meta-post</a
					>.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>Why The Tower of Babel?</h2>
			<p>
				First, I'd like to credit the artist, Pieter Bruegel the Elder, for his work. To my untrained eye, both at age 12, and today, it looks incredible. 

				<br /><br />
				The Doylist reason I use The Little Tower of Babel as a profile picture is that I thought it looked cool as a child. It stuck with me, and I started using it as a sort of leitmotif.
				<br /><br />
				The Watsonian reason is that I've always found the story of the Tower of Babel fascinating. I'm aware the moral ought to be a warning against hubris, but I took a rather different lesson.
				<br /><br />
				We were a single people once. 
				<br /><br />
				Circumstances forced this to change, but one day, we might again stand united in a common goal and struggle. 
				<br /> 
				As a child, and even now, I find that idea glorious. 
			</p>
		</section>
	</article>
</Layout>

<style>
	.about-content {
		font-family:
			"Merriweather",
			-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
			"Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
		font-size: 11pt;
		font-weight: 300;
		line-height: 1.6;
		width: 100%;
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.about-heading {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.about-heading .title {
		font-family:
			"Antic",
			-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
			"Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
		font-size: 26pt;
		font-weight: 400;
		line-height: 1.15;
		color: #000;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about-heading .subtitle {
		font-family:
			"Merriweather",
			-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto,
			"Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
		font-size: 15pt;
		font-weight: 300;
		line-height: 1.15;
		color: #666;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	h1 {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		font-size: 2rem;
	}

	section {
		margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
	}

	h2 {
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
		color: var(--h2-color);
	}

	p {
		line-height: 1.8;
		color: #8c8c8c;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}

	section:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	/* About page hero */
	.about-hero {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		gap: 2rem;
		align-items: center;
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
	}

	.hero-left {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.hero-image {
		width: 75%;
		max-width: 420px;
		height: auto;
		border-radius: 8px;
		object-fit: cover;
	}

	.hero-right h2 {
		text-align: left;
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 780px) {
		.about-hero {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			text-align: center;
		}

		.hero-right p {
			text-align: left;
		}

		.hero-right {
			order: 2;
		}

		.hero-left {
			order: 1;
		}
	}

</style>

